#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kbruch; is a small program to practice calculating with fractions. "
"Therefore 4 different exercises are offered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Fraction Task - in this exercise you have to solve a given fraction task. "
"You have to enter numerator and denominator. This is the main exercise."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Comparison - in this exercise you have to compare the size of 2 given "
"fractions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Conversion - in this exercise you have to convert a given number into a "
"fraction."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Factorization - in this exercise you have to factorize a given number into "
"its prime factors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In all different exercises &kbruch; will generate a task and the user has to "
"solve it. The program checks the input and gives a feedback about it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kbruch; counts how many tasks were solved at all and how many tasks were "
"solved correctly. The statistics are shown to the user, but this part of the "
"main window can be hidden. The user can reset the statistics at any point."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kbruch; is very compact and focuses on the core idea of a task generator. "
"An online help system provides context-sensitive help for the different "
"situations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kbruch; is free and licensed under the &GNU; Public License."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kbruch;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here is a screenshot of &kbruch;'s main screen:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kbruch; main screen, directly after the start"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kbruch; main screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All action takes place in this screen. This ensures that &kbruch; is easy to "
"use even for young users! The main screen is separated into 5 parts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the menubar with the 3 menus <guimenu>Task</guimenu>, <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> and <guimenu>Help</guimenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the toolbar, where you can set the difficulty for the tasks given in the "
"<guimenu>Fraction Task</guimenu> exercise"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "the exercise chooser, where you can switch between the different exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "the task part, where you have to enter the result of the given task"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the statistical part, where you can see how many tasks have been solved "
"correctly or attempted"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First you have to choose an exercise in the exercise chooser on the left "
"side of the window. The task part will change according to the chosen task. "
"The settings in the toolbar will be enabled, if you have chosen the exercise "
"<guimenu>Fraction Task</guimenu>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will find an icon to generate a new task in the toolbar as well. This "
"action is also available in the menu <menuchoice><guimenu>Task</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New Task</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. This action is "
"always enabled. If you have not solved the currently given task, a new task "
"is generated and the given task is counted as not correctly solved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can hide the statistic part by dragging the vertical separator to the "
"right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you terminate &kbruch; the currently chosen exercise will be saved and "
"restored on next startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Statistical Part"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this part of the main screen you can see:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "how many tasks have been solved"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid "how many tasks have been solved correctly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid "how many tasks have been solved incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can reset the statistics by clicking on the <guimenu>Reset</guimenu> "
"button under the figures."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The statistics will be saved on &kbruch;'s termination and restored on next "
"startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Settings Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this part of the main screen you can adjust some general settings for "
"task display. To open this dialog use <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kbruch;</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&kbruch; settings dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&kbruch; settings dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the top part of the dialog you can choose a font for displaying. In the "
"lower part you can choose colors for the different parts of a mathematical "
"expression. You can set wether to show the mixed number notation in the "
"result. This notation is not known everywhere and can be disabled therefore."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:228
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The settings will be saved on &kbruch;'s termination and restored on the "
"next startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exercises"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exercise Fraction Task"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to solve a given task. Therefor you have to enter "
"numerator and denominator. The difficulty of the generated task can be "
"adjusted by the task parameters described below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "Task Parameters"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:249
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are 3 parameters which influence the difficulty of the generated tasks:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "Terms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The number of terms (separate fractions) given in each task. From 2 to 5, "
"inclusive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Max. main denominator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The highest number &kbruch; will use as the main denominator in the tasks it "
"sets. From a minimum of 10 to a maximum of 50."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Operations"
msgstr "Operacions"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Operations which should be used in the task: <guilabel>Addition/Subtraction</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>Multiplication/Division</guilabel> or <guilabel>All "
"Operations Mixed</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have changed the parameters you have to click on the <guimenu>New "
"Task</guimenu> button in the toolbar to generate a task which uses the new "
"parameters. You can also call this action from the menubar with "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Task</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Task</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your selection of the maximum main denominator will be reset to a default "
"value every time you change the number of terms. So you should change the "
"number of terms first and then select the maximum main denominator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have not solved the current task and call the <guimenu>New Task</"
"guimenu> action, the task will be counted as not solved correctly. To "
"prevent this you have to change the parameters after you solved the task but "
"before generating a new one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The chosen parameters will be saved on &kbruch;'s termination and restored "
"on next startup."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "Solving Tasks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have solved a given task, you need to enter the result into the "
"two input boxes. In the upper box you enter the numerator and in the lower "
"box the denominator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the result is negative, you can enter a minus sign in front of the "
"numerator or denominator. If the result is 0, just type a 0 in the numerator "
"input field. If the result has a denominator of 1, you can leave the lower "
"box empty."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered the result you should click the <guibutton>Check "
"Task</guibutton> button below the input boxes. &kbruch; will check your "
"input and present the correct result. Therefore the screen changes a little, "
"as you can see in the screenshot:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:319
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Checked Task</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Checked Task</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:329
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This task was solved correctly. The correct value is shown in 2 different "
"forms. The second form just in front of the word <guilabel>CORRECT</"
"guilabel> is only used in some countries and must be read as 2 + 1/5 in the "
"given case."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You always have to enter the result reduced, because most teachers only give "
"all points to reduced results. &kbruch; will show you a short message like "
"the one in the screenshot below, if you enter the correct result unreduced."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Unreduced Result</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Unreduced Result</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To continue with the next task, click on the <guimenu>Next Task</guimenu> "
"button. If you want to change the parameters for the next task please do "
"this before clicking on the <guimenu>Next Task</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Exercise Comparison</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to compare 2 given fractions. You have to choose "
"the bigger fraction of both by selecting the correct comparison sign."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Exercise Comparison</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Exercise Comparison</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:381
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"First choose the correct comparison sign. To toggle the comparison sign, you "
"have to click on the button showing the comparison sign. After you have "
"chosen the comparison sign click on the <guimenu>Check Task</guimenu> "
"button. &kbruch; will check your input and present the correct result. After "
"this step you will get to the next task by clicking on the <guimenu>Next "
"Task</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:391
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Exercise Conversion</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to convert a given number into a fraction. You "
"have to enter numerator and denominator."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:398
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Exercise Conversion</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Exercise Conversion</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the left side of the equal sign in the screenshot above you can see a "
"recurring decimal. This means, that the fraction shown as a decimal has a "
"repeating part. The repeating part is marked with the small bar above the "
"numbers. Those numbers repeat ad infinitum."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered the numerator and denominator click on the "
"<guimenu>Check Task</guimenu> button. &kbruch; will check your input and "
"present the correct result. After this step you will get to the next task by "
"clicking on the <guimenu>Next Task</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Do not forget to enter the result reduced. Unreduced results will be counted "
"as solved not correctly."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Exercise Factorization</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this exercise you have to factorize a given number into its prime "
"factors. You have to enter all prime factors of the number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Exercise Factorization</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Exercise Factorization</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:448
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can enter a factor by clicking on the prime <guimenu>factor buttons</"
"guimenu>. The currently entered prime factors will be shown in the field "
"next to the number to be factorized. You can remove the last entered prime "
"factor by clicking on the <guimenu>Remove Last Factor</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:453
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you have entered all prime factors click on the <guimenu>Check Task</"
"guimenu> button. &kbruch; will check your input and present the correct "
"result. After this step you will get to the next task by clicking on the "
"<guimenu>Next Task</guimenu> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the screenshot at the top of this page you can see a <quote>*</quote> "
"between the prime factors. This is the multiplication sign. The product of "
"all prime factors must be the number you try to factorize."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:466
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You have to enter all prime factors even when a prime factor repeats several "
"times. Example: As prime factors of number 18 you have to enter 2, 3 and 3."
msgstr ""

